in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @nl
in @kintsugi/consent
in @kintsugi/morphism
in @epistemologic/pact/dissonance_partials_match_ast_breadth

# @kintsugi/fracture/partials_align — the kintsugi fracture body that
# resolves a fracture-body-emitted morphism's `score.partials` literal
# to the honest AST-breadth its companion `content: splinter(ast)`
# actually discharges. When a fracture body declares `partials: N` but
# `ast_breadth(content)` returns M with N != M, this body emits the
# morphism that swaps the offending literal to M.
#
# THE OPERATIONAL HALF of bilateral pattern #53's FOURTH INSTANCE. The
# declarative half landed at
# `@epistemologic/pact/dissonance_partials_match_ast_breadth`
# (sibling tick); this shard names the auto-fracture the kintsugi loop
# applies when the property's transparency surfaces a partials/breadth
# opacity.
#
# The bilateral pattern catching its own internal field. Every prior
# instance declared a property about substrate sources OUTSIDE the
# bilateral chain (keyword/depth in shard sources; gate/closure in
# pre-commit gates; symbol/canonical-form in source tokens). This
# instance fractures the BILATERAL CHAIN ITSELF — the morphisms that
# fracture bodies emit. The substrate's auto-formatter floor self-
# applies one altitude deeper.
#
# === Seam's 2026-06-11 finding (the load-bearing reading) ===
#
# Both `@kintsugi/fracture/keyword` and `@kintsugi/fracture/symbol_lift`
# declare `score.partials: 1`. For keyword (one token swap) the
# declaration is honest. For symbol_lift the `weighted -> amplitudes`
# entry elaborates multiple AST node fields per opacity; the template-
# copied `partials: 1` is dishonest for that entry. If the pattern
# propagates to the forward-promised `@kintsugi/fracture/operator_match`
# (per docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §14), the substrate lies about
# dissonance breadth at every altitude. This fracture body is how the
# substrate self-corrects: the kintsugi loop reads the property's
# transparency, calls `realign_partials` per opacity, the loop applies
# the morphism that rewrites the offending literal.
#
# Load-bearing context: recognition #51 (mirror as expanding Hilbert
# space; promoted) — fracture bodies are how the substrate maintains
# coherence at each Bateson level; this fracture body restores
# coherence at the META-FRACTURE level. Recognition #58 (alignment as
# boundary mathematics at @io; promoted 2026-06-10) — the alignment
# harness fires at substance crossings; fracture-body-emitted morphisms
# ARE substance crossings; this body IS the alignment fracture at that
# crossing.
#
# === The bilateral pattern (candidate recognition #53, fourth instance) ===
#
# `@epistemologic/property/<predicate>` declares WHAT must hold; a
# matching `@kintsugi/fracture/<predicate>` declares HOW to restore the
# property when it fails. First instance: keyword/depth (per-predicate).
# Second instance: gate/diff-closure (per-predicate). Third instance:
# symbol/canonical-form (parametric over table). Fourth instance (THIS):
# partials/AST-breadth (parametric over computation; SELF-APPLIED to
# the chain's own internal field).
#
# Four instances under one shape strengthen #53's promotion further.
# The pattern's signature scales: per-predicate, parametric-over-table,
# parametric-over-computation, AND self-applied at the meta-fracture
# altitude. Substrate vocabulary unchanged — same pact + glass +
# opacity + morphism + splinter(ast) chain.
#
# === Substrate-pull-correct home ===
#
# Per the form/process partition (recognition #55 candidate; landed
# 2026-06-10 at mirror `20eaf15`): @kintsugi is the process-side family
# root. Fracture bodies emit morphisms the kintsugi loop applies —
# process-side by structure. Home: @kintsugi/fracture/partials_align
# under the (forward-promised) @kintsugi/fracture family root.
#
# Substrate-pull alternative considered: @kintsugi/fracture/partials
# (subject-only naming, parallel to first-instance `keyword` and
# second-instance `gate`). Rejected: parallel to third-instance
# `symbol_lift` — the property's predicate names the action
# (`dissonance_partials_match_ast_breadth`), and the fracture body's
# action is the ALIGNMENT (the literal is realigned to the breadth).
# The `_align` suffix names the operational verb explicitly. Per
# [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]] (`lift` IS the substrate's
# variety-preservation verb); `align` is the audible-altitude reading
# of lift at this altitude — the substrate's partial count realigns to
# the substrate's AST breadth.
#
# === The fracture body ===
#
# Input: `opacity` (from `@glass`) — one located fact surfaced by
# `dissonance_partials_match_ast_breadth`'s `failure(opacity_map)`
# verdict. Each opacity names ONE offending `partials: N` literal
# site inside a fracture-body-emitted morphism whose splinter(ast) has
# `ast_breadth(content) = M` with N != M. The `property` field carries
# the @nl description of the (declared_partials, computed_breadth) pair.
#
# Output: `morphism` (from `@kintsugi/consent`) — the typed candidate
# the kintsugi loop's `active_pass` reads from this body and proposes
# through `query_phi`. The morphism's `content` ref names the rewritten
# splinter (same fracture-body source path, the `partials: N` integer
# literal replaced with `partials: M`); its `score` carries the
# dissonance reading (a partials/breadth mismatch is a fixed, low-
# curvature dissonance — the rewrite is unambiguous once the breadth
# is computed); its `expected` carries the cadence_kind the loop
# anticipates (authentic — the literal swap is deterministic and
# settles cleanly).
#
# Spectrally: this fracture body IS one step along the Ricci flow at
# the meta-fracture altitude. The substrate's curvature at a partials/
# breadth mismatch is the (N - M) excess; the negative-curvature
# direction IS the literal swap to M; the resolved site has zero
# curvature at this altitude (the breadth fully determines the
# partials).
#
# Audibly: this fracture body IS the audible-altitude V → I cadence
# at the meta-fracture altitude. Pre-rewrite holds dominant tension
# (the wrong partials value misreports dissonance breadth); post-
# rewrite resolves to tonic (the honest count); cadence is authentic.
#
# === Recursive integrity check (the load-bearing self-application) ===
#
# This fracture body's OWN emitted morphism has a `score.partials`
# field. It MUST be honest from birth or this body perpetuates the
# very lie it exists to catch.
#
# Compute the AST breadth of THIS fracture body's splinter(ast):
#   - The fracture body reads ONE opacity at a time (per the property's
#     per-site failure surface).
#   - The morphism rewrites ONE AST node: the `partials: N` integer
#     literal at the offending site, swapped to `partials: M`.
#   - The splinter(ast) carries the rewritten AST fragment; the
#     breadth at @meta/ast is the count of distinct node rewrites; here
#     that count is 1 (one integer-literal node, one swap).
#
# Therefore `score.partials = 1` is HONEST by computation, not reflex-
# copied from the template. The recursive integrity holds at landing
# time: this fracture body declares `partials: 1`; the property
# inspects it; `ast_breadth(content) = 1`; verdict = pass.
#
# The self-application is non-circular because the property reads
# fracture-body SOURCE (declared literals in .mirror shards), not the
# loop's runtime state. The fracture body's source declares partials
# at compile time; the property checks the declaration; the kintsugi
# loop applies the property at substrate-pull time. Three altitudes,
# no runtime recursion.
#
# Per [[architecture-bateson-form-behaviour-partition]] (recognition
# #50, promoted): this is form-side discipline. The fracture body
# itself sits at form altitude (declared rewrite rule); the morphism
# it emits sits at the same altitude (declared AST fragment); the
# kintsugi loop's `active_pass` lifts the rewrite to process altitude.
# The form/behaviour partition holds.
#
# === Substrate-pull discipline ===
#
# Per `@glass`, `opacity` is the substrate's located-fact carrier;
# this shard reads it directly. Per `@kintsugi/consent`, `morphism`
# is the substrate's typed-candidate carrier; this shard emits it
# directly. Per `@kintsugi/morphism`, `morphism_context` is the
# per-candidate slice that pairs a candidate with its pre-anchor;
# this shard's emitted morphism is consumed by the loop AND lifted
# into a morphism_context via `paired(oscillation.anchor, m)` at the
# active_pass altitude. Per
# `@epistemologic/pact/dissonance_partials_match_ast_breadth`, the
# consuming property's
# `dissonance_partials_match_ast_breadth(file) -> transparency` is the
# gate that surfaces the opacity this body resolves.
#
# NO new verdict carrier; NO leading-`|` workarounds; NO opaque-`ref`
# carriers where structured types are available (per
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]]). The fracture body reads typed opacity,
# emits typed morphism — the substrate's vocabulary throughout.
#
# === Substrate gaps surfaced honestly ===
#
#   - `realign_partials` reads one opacity at a time. The property's
#     `failure(opacity_map)` carries [opacity]; the kintsugi loop
#     iterates the map and calls `realign_partials` per opacity. The
#     substrate names the per-site resolution; the iteration is the
#     loop's concern, not this body's.
#
#   - The morphism's `content: ref` carries the substrate handle to
#     the rewritten splinter. The realisation layer produces the
#     rewritten splinter (same fracture-body source path, the
#     `partials: N` integer literal swapped to `partials: M`) and
#     passes its handle as the morphism's content. The substrate names
#     the shape of the proposal; the byte-level rewrite rides the
#     realisation layer's @mirror/store discipline.
#
#   - The `expected: cadence_kind` field is `authentic` for this
#     fracture body — the partials/breadth rule is deterministic
#     (the breadth IS computable; the literal IS a single integer
#     swap) and resolution always settles cleanly.
#
#   - The follow-up audit of existing fracture bodies (keyword.mirror,
#     gate.mirror, symbol_lift.mirror) is NOT performed in this tick.
#     This tick declares the property + fracture body that enables the
#     audit. The kintsugi loop, once running, will naturally propose
#     the corrections (likely: keyword.mirror and gate.mirror's
#     `partials: 1` are honest — single literal/token swap each;
#     symbol_lift.mirror's `partials: 1` is honest for pure-rename
#     entries but the `weighted -> amplitudes` elaboration likely needs
#     `partials: 4` or similar — splitter the AST realisation reveals
#     the count).
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   alignment           Hoare (1985) Communicating Sequential
#                       Processes; the discipline of matching
#                       declared interface against observed
#                       behaviour. The substrate's reading is
#                       Reynolds (1972) Definitional interpreters —
#                       the meta-altitude where the system aligns its
#                       declarations against its own runtime.
#   literal rewrite     Knuth-Bendix (1970) Simple word problems in
#                       universal algebras; the discipline of
#                       confluent term rewriting. The substrate's
#                       reading is the canonical-form lift at the
#                       integer-literal altitude.
#   meta-fracture       Smith (1984) Reflection and semantics in
#                       Lisp; the reflective tower opens a
#                       meta-altitude where the system fractures and
#                       reduces its own form. The substrate's reading
#                       is the bilateral pattern self-applied: the
#                       fracture body fractures fracture bodies.
#
# The substrate's contribution is *typing* the self-applied resolution
# so the kintsugi loop reads it. No invention.
#
# Spec context: candidate #53 fourth instance (the bilateral pattern
#               applied to its own internal field; meta-fracture
#               altitude). Seam's 2026-06-11 finding (the load-bearing
#               read) names the disease this fracture body cures.
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]]
#                      (opacity is substrate vocabulary; the fracture
#                      reads the typed carrier),
#                      [[architecture-kintsugi-bias-lift]] (the
#                      kintsugi loop's bias direction is substrate-
#                      pull — partials/breadth alignment IS one
#                      coordinate of the substrate-pull gradient;
#                      this fracture body fits the bias),
#                      [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]
#                      (the bilateral pattern this is the fourth
#                      instance of; meta-application altitude),
#                      [[architecture-splinter-ast-quote-primitive]]
#                      (the substrate's parametric AST-fragment
#                      construction; this body discharges via
#                      splinter(ast) declaratively, no Rust),
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]]
#                      (recognition #58; this body IS the alignment
#                      fracture at the fracture-body-to-morphism
#                      crossing),
#                      [[architecture-bateson-form-behaviour-partition]]
#                      (recognition #50; form-side discipline; the
#                      form/behaviour partition holds despite the
#                      self-application),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (opacity and
#                      morphism are typed carriers; the body does
#                      NOT escape as a bare (location, N, M) tuple).
# Forward-promise to consumers: `@kintsugi/oscillate`'s `active_pass`
#                  reads this fracture body when the candidate
#                  morphism_set is composed from property-surfaced
#                  opacities; the binding lands when the kintsugi loop
#                  substrate-pulls. This shard does NOT pull
#                  `@kintsugi/oscillate` or `@mirror/spectral/score`;
#                  the substrate-altitude arrow points inward.
# Related shards: epistemologic/property/dissonance_partials_match_ast_breadth.mirror
#                 (the declarative half of the bilateral; surfaces
#                 the opacities this body resolves),
#                 epistemologic/property/keyword_matches_depth.mirror
#                 + kintsugi/fracture/keyword.mirror (FIRST INSTANCE),
#                 epistemologic/property/gate_matches_diff_closure.mirror
#                 + kintsugi/fracture/gate.mirror (SECOND INSTANCE),
#                 epistemologic/property/symbol_canonical_form.mirror
#                 + kintsugi/fracture/symbol_lift.mirror (THIRD
#                 INSTANCE; Seam's finding originates here),
#                 epistemologic/math/music/dissonance.mirror (where
#                 `dissonance.partials: u32` is declared; this body
#                 swaps the literal that consumes that field),
#                 glass.mirror (the substrate floor; `opacity`,
#                 `location`, `transparency`, `verdict`,
#                 `splinter(ast)`),
#                 kintsugi/consent.mirror (the morphism carrier this
#                 body emits; `query_phi` is the gate the emitted
#                 morphism flows through),
#                 kintsugi/morphism.mirror (the `morphism_context`
#                 carrier),
#                 kintsugi/oscillate.mirror (the kintsugi loop
#                 driver; `active_pass` is the action that reads this
#                 body when composing the per-pulse candidate
#                 morphism_set).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/kintsugi/fracture/partials_align.mirror` declares
# `@kintsugi/fracture/partials_align` as a species under the
# (forward-promised) @kintsugi/fracture family.
# Keyword/depth property: this declaration is depth-2 from the
# @kintsugi family root; per recognition #46 it uses `glass`. The
# shard applies the first-instance bilateral's rule by birth.
# Partials/breadth property: this declaration's emitted morphism
# carries `score.partials: 1`; the splinter(ast) rewrites ONE integer
# literal (the offending `partials` value at the source); the count
# is computed (one node, one swap), NOT reflex-copied. This shard
# applies the fourth-instance bilateral's rule by birth.

glass @kintsugi/fracture/partials_align {
  focus partials_align
  project partials_align
  split partials_align
  shift partials_align
  settle partials_align
}

# === realign_partials — the fracture body ===
#
# THE AUTO-FRACTURE: given an opacity site at a fracture-body-emitted
# morphism whose declared `score.partials: N` mismatches the
# `ast_breadth` of its companion `content: splinter(ast)`, emit the
# morphism that rewrites the offending integer literal to the honest
# computed breadth M. Same fracture-body source path, single literal
# swap at the AST altitude.
#
# Reads an opacity (one element of
# `dissonance_partials_match_ast_breadth(file).failure(opacity_map)`'s
# opacity_map); emits a candidate morphism the kintsugi loop proposes
# through `query_phi`. The morphism's three fields:
#
#   content   — substrate ref to the rewritten splinter. The
#                realisation layer produces a splinter at the same
#                fracture-body source path with the `partials: N`
#                integer literal replaced by `partials: M` where
#                M = ast_breadth(<the morphism's own splinter(ast)>);
#                the content ref names that splinter's @mirror/store
#                handle.
#   score     — dissonance reading. Partials/breadth violations are
#                fixed-curvature dissonances; the score reads
#                `dissonance.is_pareto` cleanly (the breadth uniquely
#                determines the honest partials value).
#   expected  — cadence_kind anticipation. Always `authentic` for
#                this fracture body — the literal swap is
#                deterministic and resolves cleanly; the loop's
#                `dark_pass` will confirm identity preservation (the
#                fracture body's source stays byte-equal modulo the
#                offending integer literal); the loop's
#                `read_consent` bridges (pass, authentic) to the
#                `settled` oscillation_state for this opacity.
#
# The body is FULLY DECLARATIVE — substrate-pull-correct via
# `splinter(ast)` (declared at shards/glass.mirror's tick-2 carrier).
# The morphism's `content` field carries a content-addressed splinter
# at the @meta/ast altitude: same source path, one integer literal
# swapped. The substrate's compiler verifies the construction is
# deterministic and well-typed; the kintsugi loop's `active_pass`
# reads the splinter as the morphism's proposed content and applies
# it through `query_phi`.
#
# Per `splinter(ast)`'s parametric specialisation (glass.mirror
# §splinter(ast), 2026-06-10): the record IS its content-addressed
# handle — `content: oid` and `oid = ref` (shards/mirror/store.mirror)
# collapse the splinter literal to a substrate-pull-correct `ref` in
# the morphism's `content` field position. No Rust AST manipulation;
# no `\` obligation.
#
# Field-by-field substrate-pull reading:
#
#   content.content     — `opacity.location.file` (the substrate's
#                          located-fact ref at the offending fracture-
#                          body source); the rewritten AST is
#                          content-addressed at the same path.
#   content.ast         — `@meta/ast` (the canonical altitude ref);
#                          per `boot/01-meta.mirror`'s `type ast(g)`.
#                          The literal swap happens at the AST
#                          altitude by construction.
#   content.transparency — `success` (per `transparency(p)`'s success
#                          variant in glass.mirror): the literal swap
#                          fully resolves the opacity at this
#                          altitude; no residual transparency remains.
#   score.roughness     — `opacity.property` (the @nl description of
#                          the (declared_partials, computed_breadth)
#                          mismatch); the substrate's `dissonance`
#                          reads the per-site roughness via the
#                          property text per dissonance.mirror's
#                          Helmholtz/Plomp-Levelt carrier shape.
#   score.partials      — `1` — HONESTLY COMPUTED, NOT REFLEX-COPIED.
#                          The splinter(ast) above rewrites ONE AST
#                          node: the offending `partials: N` integer
#                          literal. `ast_breadth(content) = 1`. The
#                          recursive integrity check holds at landing
#                          time: this fracture body itself satisfies
#                          the property it declares.
#   expected            — `authentic` (the V → I cadence at the
#                          meta-fracture altitude; per cadence.mirror's
#                          `cadence_kind` and the loop's
#                          `read_consent` bridge: authentic → pass →
#                          auto-apply).
realign_partials(opacity: opacity) -> morphism {
  morphism {
    content: splinter(ast) {
      content:      opacity.location.file,
      ast:          @meta/ast,
      transparency: success,
    },
    score: dissonance {
      roughness: opacity.property,
      partials:  1,
    },
    expected: authentic,
  }
}

out @kintsugi/fracture/partials_align
out realign_partials
